======================================================================================================================
THE DECISION
======================================================================================================================
  Rule, fixed before the run: over the NON-IDENTITY cells on the full
  held-out block, build a copula only if a MAJORITY have a PIT interval
  excluding zero AND |PIT spearman| > 0.125.

  EXCLUDED as an identity: 30m/0.5h (PIT -1.0000, raw -1.0000) -- arithmetic, not data.
  9 cells decide. 9 PIT intervals exclude zero; 9 also clear |rho| > 0.125.
  Largest |PIT spearman|: -0.8595 at 30m/1h [-0.868, -0.848], raw -0.8536 at the same cell.

  VERDICT: CONDITIONAL DEPENDENCE IS THERE. A majority of cells clear
  both bars after the features, so a copula on the EXISTING marginals
  is worth building -- as its own strategy-phase deliverable. It will
  not move one number on the calibration scoreboard.

